# Copy to .env.local. Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values reach the browser — there are
# deliberately none (IMPLEMENTATION_V2.md §2B.2 D2: the browser never calls the
# backend, so it needs no API URL).

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Backend origin. Read by next.config.ts at BUILD TIME for the /api/v1 proxy
# rewrite, and server-side by lib/api/client.ts. Changing it requires a rebuild.
#
# No trailing slash, no path. A production build REFUSES to start without it,
# rather than compiling localhost into a deployed bundle.
API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# An ADDITIONAL allowed origin for the CSRF check. Not required, and normally
# left unset.
#
# `lib/http/same-origin.ts` compares the request's Origin against its own Host,
# so the check works on whatever port `next dev` bound to and on Vercel preview
# URLs, whose origin is not known at build time. Set this only for a deployment
# behind a proxy that rewrites Host.
#
# (Until P20 this was documented as required, and mismatching it turned every
# mutation into a 500 — which is exactly why it is no longer required.)
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app
